R87 - team / league row allocation constraints (creation / growth inputs) measured on every committed main-database anchor
(X360 / PS3 08-Legacy, PS4 15-21). Read-only over `anchors/`.

Per anchor:
  teams      `exhibitionteams`: `index` field range, rows, table capacity (`max_records`) vs current rows (headroom), free index values
             inside the declared range that no row holds, the `league` / `conference` / `division` / `leaguegroup` / `teamtype` value
             censuses (what a new row must choose from), `arenaid` coverage by the arena index set;
  keyed      every field named team / teamid / juniorteam / rivalteam / ahlaffiliate / team_id in every table: coverage of its non-zero
             values by the team index set (>= 0.95 = index reference), rows per team (min / median / max over the teams that have rows,
             and how many teams have none) - the rows a new team would need in that table - and the table's headroom;
  arenas     `exhibitionarena`: index range, rows, capacity, free indexes;
  schedule   every table whose name contains 'schedule': rows, capacity, headroom;
  leagues    `stockleagues` / `exhibitionleagues` where present: rows, capacity, id ranges.
Usage: python r87_team_row_allocation.py <out.json>
